<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Jackson returns two weeks after her first visit. The CT of the chest two days after that visit showed enlarged hilar and mediastinal lymph nodes and small nodules along the airways in both upper lobes. EBUS-guided needle aspiration five days ago found non-necrotizing granulomas in three lymph node stations, with negative stains for mycobacteria and fungi; cultures are growing nothing so far. The interferon-gamma release assay and HIV test from the first visit were negative. She stopped the over-the-counter calcium and vitamin D tablets as advised. Her breathlessness and cough are unchanged, and she had one more spell of palpitations while singing at church. She has postponed her concerts for the next three weeks. Dr. Asante-Miller saw her this morning, and she had full lung function tests. She has had no thoughts of self-harm. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Tissue</td><td>Non-necrotizing granulomas at stations 4R, 7 and 11L; stains negative; cultures pending; lavage lymphocytes 32 percent, CD4 to CD8 ratio 5.2</td></tr><tr><td>Infection excluded so far</td><td>Interferon-gamma release assay and HIV negative; acid-fast and fungal stains negative</td></tr><tr><td>Lung function</td><td>FVC 74 percent and DLCO 62 percent of predicted</td></tr><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>Breathlessness and cough unchanged; one more spell of palpitations</td></tr><tr><td>Work</td><td>Concerts postponed for three weeks</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

