    <code code="11450-4" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Problem List"/>
    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Breathlessness on exertion and a dry cough for three months, worse on tour, with tiredness and chest tightness; she can no longer hold long phrases; bilateral hilar lymph node enlargement on today&apos;s chest radiograph; granulomas were reported at an abdominal operation twelve years ago, with no pathology report available: sarcoidosis must be confirmed by tissue and other causes excluded</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R06.09</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to the documented breathlessness during performances and the 1952 granulomas. Superseded by the tissue diagnosis at the consultation.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Palpitations with two spells of light-headedness while singing; ECG today: sinus rhythm with first-degree atrioventricular block (PR 240 ms) and frequent ventricular ectopic beats: cardiac involvement must be looked for</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R00.2</td><td>S — Synthetic finding; superseded when cardiac sarcoidosis was diagnosed.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Hypercalcemia: calcium 10.8 mg/dL with a high 1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D and a low 25-hydroxyvitamin D, while taking an over-the-counter calcium and vitamin D supplement; creatinine slightly raised</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>E83.52</td><td>S — Synthetic finding; resolved on treatment.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Pulmonary sarcoidosis with hilar and mediastinal lymph node involvement (Scadding stage II), confirmed by non-necrotizing granulomas on EBUS-guided lymph node aspiration with negative stains and cultures; mild restriction and reduced diffusing capacity; synthetic modern detail linked to her documented sarcoidosis</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>D86.2</td><td>S — Synthetic histology, stage and lung function; her biographer reports a diagnosis of sarcoidosis after granulomas were found at an operation (D, probable).</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

